# ── NEVER COMMIT: anything tied to a real target ──────────────────────
#
# NOTE ON SYNTAX: gitignore has no trailing comments. A line like
#   .tenanttrace/    # run artifacts
# is a pattern containing spaces and a hash — it matches nothing, and the rule
# silently does not exist. Every comment here is therefore on its own line.
# (This exact mistake shipped in an earlier draft of this file and would have
# published real findings.)

# real base_url + the names of your credential env vars.
# Anchored to the repo root and covering per-target variants: a config named
# for one application (tenanttrace.myapp.toml) is exactly as sensitive as the
# default one, and the narrower pattern let one through.
# The fixtures' own configs live under fixtures/ and stay tracked.
/tenanttrace.toml
/tenanttrace.*.toml
!/tenanttrace.example.toml

# run artifacts: discovered leaks, request/response pairs, canaries
.tenanttrace/

# docker compose demo output — findings, not source
reports/

# your per-app seeder adapters, except the documented example
seeders/*.py
!seeders/example_seeder.py

*.har
*.postman_collection.json

# NOTE: `.tenanttrace-baseline.json` is intentionally NOT ignored. The baseline
# is the list of findings a team has consciously accepted, so it belongs in the
# repository where its diffs get reviewed. It stores fingerprints and titles
# only — never canary values, tokens, or response bodies (ADR-0007).

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# ── Tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.hypothesis/

# ── Env / secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── Editors / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Generated on every Pages deploy by `make demo-site`; see the Makefile.
/docs/site/report-*.html
